+++ b/docs/platform/beam-inspection-evidence.md
@@ -0,0 +1,153 @@
+# BEAM inspection validation
+
+Validated on 2026-10-20 against Dash base `ea45f9505d84f66d5fefeee64f71c13a0173cb98`
+plus the inspection working changes. This record separates local execution,
+packaged execution and actual deployment evidence.
+
+## Results
+
+| Surface                                             | Local Nix environment             | Packaged image                                        | Actual Fly deployment            |
+| --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |
+| Exact node confirmation and bounded RPC             | Passed                            | Passed                                                | Not checked: CLI unauthenticated |
+| Erlang console and client disconnect                | Passed on disposable VM           | Passed on Dash VM                                     | Not checked                      |
+| IEx and client disconnect                           | Target packaging checked in image | Passed on Dash VM                                     | Not checked                      |
+| Process memory/mailbox/status/reductions/MFA stacks | Passed                            | Passed                                                | Not checked                      |
+| Supervisor children and ETS metadata                | Backend tests passed              | Passed                                                | Not checked                      |
+| Recon resources and bounded tracing                 | Passed                            | Passed                                                | Not checked                      |
+| Trace cleanup after observed client interruption    | Passed                            | Normal completion passed; interruption tested locally | Not checked                      |
+| Existing application-pool READ ONLY transaction     | Passed                            | Passed                                                | Not checked                      |
+| Disposable exact-key repair and verified rollback   | Passed                            | Passed                                                | Not attempted                    |
+| Stopped node / wrong cookie / missing module        | Passed generic client checks      | Shared client packaged; no deployment fault injection | Not attempted                    |
+| Cookie ownership/mode and loopback listeners        | Same-user normal cookie           | Explicit assertions passed                            | Not checked                      |
+| Public `/api/ready`                                 | Outside this check                | Outside this check                                    | HTTP 200                         |
+
+The Fly HTTP request read only the response status. `flyctl machine list --app
+dash-abertura --json` failed with `no access token available`. No Machine was
+selected or attached. No deployment, restart, secret update, deployed write or
+customer query was performed. HTTP 200 proves public readiness at observation
+time; it does not prove distribution or this integration is deployed.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+Run from the repository root:
+
+```sh
+nix develop --command bash tools/scripts/check-inspection.sh
+nix develop --command python3 tools/scripts/check-inspection-image.py IMAGE
+nix develop --command bash tools/scripts/inspection-queries.sh check
+nix develop --command python3 tools/scripts/check-telemetry.py
+nix develop --command bash -c 'cd backend/api && gleam test'
+nix flake check
+```
+
+The local acceptance owns a fresh PostgreSQL 16 database. It enrolls a new database
+instance, applies explicit Cigogne membership migrations, then starts actual Dash
+main with fixture identity configuration. It discovers `dash_auth_pool$...`,
+confirms READ ONLY and explicitly rolls back before returning its connection.
+A separate one-connection fixture verifies the same backend PID is reusable after
+both investigation and repair rehearsal.
+
+The repair result was `{ok,{rollback_proof,1,1,true}}`. It changed only a fresh
+transaction-local temporary table, using an exact key and expected old value.
+It checked affected rows and RETURNING values, verified the table disappeared
