+# Inspect the existing BEAM service
+
+Use the Nix shell for local commands. Build once with
+`nix develop --command tools/scripts/build-backend.sh`. Normal local startup
+(`nix run .#dev -- backend`) names only the service `dash_dev@127.0.0.1`.
+Builds, explicit membership migrations and database recovery remain separate,
+unnamed VMs. A fresh `gleam shell` cannot inspect the existing service.
+
+```sh
+tools/beam/beam-tool console dash_dev@127.0.0.1
+tools/beam/beam-tool iex dash_dev@127.0.0.1
+tools/beam/beam-tool rpc dash_dev@127.0.0.1 dash_abertura_backend@inspection overview '[]'
+tools/beam/beam-tool rpc dash_dev@127.0.0.1 dash_abertura_backend@inspection registered_names '[]'
+tools/beam/beam-tool rpc dash_dev@127.0.0.1 dash_abertura_backend@inspection processes '[10]'
+tools/beam/beam-tool rpc dash_dev@127.0.0.1 dash_abertura_backend@inspection ets '[]'
+tools/beam/beam-tool rpc dash_dev@127.0.0.1 dash_abertura_backend@inspection resources '[]'
+tools/beam/beam-tool rpc dash_dev@127.0.0.1 dash_abertura_backend@inspection trace '[1000,10]'
+tools/beam/beam-tool rpc dash_dev@127.0.0.1 dash_abertura_backend@inspection database '[]'
+```
+
+Every RPC confirms the exact target before calling it. Timeouts default to five
+seconds and can be explicitly bounded to at most thirty seconds. Top-level
+application errors and invocation errors exit nonzero without private payloads.
+Use RPC for automation; do not pipe commands into IEx. A successful arbitrary
+RPC is not automatically safe: use the reviewed inspection exports for scripts.
+
+The process snapshot exposes bounded metadata and stack MFAs. It omits state,
+messages, dictionaries and stack arguments. `children/1` accepts a registered name or target-generated PID string
+for a confirmed supervisor; inspect ownership before invoking it. Do not copy a client-rendered remote PID
+back as a target PID; resolve registered names on the target. Discover the
+actual generated names, including `$` suffixes. Never guess a pool name or
+print its options. Recon tracing uses an exclusive cooperative owner, a target
+side deadline and aggregate counts. It refuses existing tracing. Coordinate with
+other operators; an external tool can race the cooperative lock.
+
+Dash pins `gleam_otp` 1.3.0. Its actors support state inspection but do not
+implement `sys:replace_state`, GenServer debug tracing, code change or the
+standard termination request. Both `get_state` and `get_status` can expose
+private values. Use public Gleam domain APIs for changes, preserving validation,
+notifications, recovery admission and external-effect evidence.
+
+Leave a remote Erlang shell with Ctrl-G, then `q` at the user-switch prompt.
+Leave IEx with Ctrl-C twice. These stop the client. Never invoke `halt()`,
+`init:stop()` or `System.halt()` on the target. Verify `overview/0` after leaving.
+
+## Fly: select an existing Machine
+
+```sh
+flyctl machine list --app dash-abertura
+flyctl ssh console --app dash-abertura --machine MACHINE_ID --user app
+id
+printf '%s\n' "$FLY_MACHINE_ID" "$HOME"
+/app/tools/beam/beam-tool rpc dash@127.0.0.1 dash_abertura_backend@inspection overview '[]'
+/app/tools/beam/beam-tool console dash@127.0.0.1
+/app/tools/beam/beam-tool iex dash@127.0.0.1
+```
+
+Compare the actual Machine ID with the selection before proceeding. For scripted
+calls use the same selection with `--command` and the RPC command above. SSH
+commonly defaults to root; root and app have different cookie homes. Select app
+and verify its HOME rather than copying a cookie into a root session. Attach
+inside the selected Machine over loopback. Do not expose distribution ports,
+create an HTTP evaluation endpoint or create a replacement Machine for inspection.
+Desktop Observer/Voyager remains optional and needs a separate private connection
+plan; it is not required by this workflow.
+
+The image ships the compiled RPC client, compatible Elixir/IEx runtime modules
+and Recon. The service loads IEx code paths at startup. A laptop's IEx does not
+supply target modules. Erlang console attachment remains available independently.
+
+Before deploying this configuration, provision a distribution cookie as a Fly
+secret or a protected service-owned mount. Feed secrets from a private file,
+not a literal shell command, source file or log:
+
+```sh
+flyctl secrets import --app dash-abertura < /private/operator/beam-cookie.env
+```
+
+The private import file contains `BEAM_COOKIE=...`. Provisioning is a deliberate
+deployment action and can restart Machines; it is not read-only inspection.
+The launcher requires provisioning on Fly, writes `/home/app/.erlang.cookie`
+with mode 0600 as app, and removes the secret source from the service environment.
+A `BEAM_COOKIE_FILE` must be service-owned with mode 0400/0600. A root-owned mount
+needs a privileged initialization step that creates a private app-owned copy
+before privilege drop. Do not loosen mount permissions. Local same-user VMs use
+the normal cookie file automatically; no manual copying is needed.
+
+## Optional Voyager MCP
+
+Use Voyager for process/ETS exploration when a private desktop connection is
+already available. It is independent of the host-local console/RPC workflow.
+The current upstream connector requires OTP 27+ and the target `compiler`
+application: it compiles and loads an in-memory helper. Baseline precompiled
+RPC does not need this. The desktop app is not installed by Dash.
+
+Point an MCP client at `http://127.0.0.1:4040/mcp` on the operator's laptop.
+Discover the available schemas and confirm `node_info.node` before each probe.
+For Dash, require the exact chosen node, not whichever node the desktop last used.
+Coordinate against connection switching; use exact-target RPC for deterministic
+scripts. Start with `process_list` arguments:
+
+```json
+{
+  "limit": 5,
+  "sort_by": "memory",
+  "attrs": ["memory", "reductions", "message_queue_len"]
+}
+```
+
+Use `ets_list` for metadata. Do not automatically request state, messages,
+dictionaries, labels or ETS contents. Truncation is not redaction. Even
+`process_info` includes fields beyond Dash's reviewed projections. Keep its raw
+response out of Sinal logs and automated evidence. A small return limit does not
+bound the scan of processes or tables. Voyager does not supply domain repair,
+Recon cleanup or database transaction ownership.
+
+Voyager's SSH connector needs a verified ordinary SSH route; `flyctl ssh console`
+is not that route. Keep the default explicit-Machine SSH workflow above. No public
+distribution port or forwarded MCP endpoint is needed. Voyager MCP behavior is
+source-reviewed here, not a claimed end-to-end desktop qualification.
+
+## Database investigation and repair
+
+`database/0` finds the one existing `dash_auth_pool$...` pool. It checks out one
+connection, starts a verified read-only transaction, applies statement/lock/idle
+limits and returns only pool identity, backend PID, read-only mode and recovery
+status. It never creates a pool or returns customer rows. An absent or ambiguous
+pool is an explicit error. Keep all investigation statements within the same
+transaction; separate RPC calls cannot establish connection affinity.
+
+For a separate SQL client, use a protected libpq service/password file:
+
+```sh
+PGSERVICE=dash-readonly psql -X --set ON_ERROR_STOP=1
+```
+
+```sql
+BEGIN READ ONLY;
+SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '1s';
+SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '250ms';
+SET LOCAL idle_in_transaction_session_timeout = '2s';
+SHOW transaction_read_only;
+-- Verify on before any investigation query.
+SELECT pg_backend_pid();
+ROLLBACK;
+```
+
+For the disposable local repair rehearsal, explicitly call `rollback_probe/0`.
+It creates only a transaction-local temporary table, checks exact keys and
+expected old values, verifies affected rows and RETURNING values, then verifies
+rollback removed the table. Do not run this write rehearsal on Fly by default.
+Real repairs require domain authorization, exact keys, concurrency checks and
+postconditions. Prefer domain APIs. Never bypass recovery holds, change migration
+history or infer that a timed-out external effect failed. Follow
+[membership database ownership](membership-database.md) and
+[database recovery](database-recovery.md). Operational SQL is Squirrel-generated;
+`tools/scripts/inspection-queries.sh check` verifies freshness using a private DB.
+
+## Failed attachment
+
+- No EPMD registration: check the service launcher; ordinary Gleam starts unnamed.
+- Wrong Machine/user: verify the explicit ID, process user and HOME first.
+- Authentication failure: inspect cookie file owner/mode without reading content.
+- Name mismatch: match long versus short naming and the full target name.
+- Refused connection: check loopback EPMD/listeners, not public firewall rules.
+- Missing export or IEx: check target code paths and the shipped modules.
+- Actor sys timeout: inspect the pinned implementation before retrying.
+
+Keep diagnostics outside application Sinal logs. Automated output must omit
+credentials, customer content, headers, URLs, process state and raw exceptions.
+Record local, image and actual Fly evidence separately. See the [validation record](beam-inspection-evidence.md)
+for this integration; local tests do not establish deployed readiness.
+
+Executable acceptance uses disposable databases:
+
+```sh
+nix develop --command bash tools/scripts/check-inspection.sh
+nix develop --command python3 tools/scripts/check-inspection-image.py IMAGE
+```
